// expect: 29
// band B M1.3 gate — the k2 call-boundary composition (the bank Ruling 5).
// The yield crosses ONE intermediate frame: outer's `step()` is a non-tail
// can-yield CALL (the `+ 10` consumes it), so the boundary check parks the
// dummy, composes outer's remainder (`?? + 10`) onto the unwinding k via
// $__k_extend, and the driver's resume runs BOTH remainders through the
// composer: resume(v) = (v + 3) + 10.
//   a = resume(1) → 14; b = resume(2) → 15; arm = a + b → exit 29.
// Broken paths this pins: a missing boundary check computes 10 on the dummy
// (exit 20-ish garbage); a clobbered $yield_op misses the driver dispatch
// (backstop trap 134); a wrong composition order yields (v + 10) + 3 — same
// sum here, so the pipe twin (mn-k2-pipe, asymmetric stages) pins order.
effect Choice {
  pick() -> Int
}

handler twice {
  pick() => {
    let a = resume(1)
    let b = resume(2)
    a + b
  }
}

fn step() = pick() + 3

fn outer() = step() + 10

fn main() = { outer() } ~> twice
